<title>GERMANY: BMW SAYS 96 NET PROFIT UP TO 820 MLN DMK.</title>
<headline>BMW SAYS 96 NET PROFIT UP TO 820 MLN DMK.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31 1996.</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group net profit			   820     vs 692</p>
<p>    Group profit from ord activities     1,660   vs 1,367</p>
<p>    Dividend (marks)			   15	vs 13.50</p>
<p>    Dividend on preferred shares (marks) 16	vs 14.50</p>
<p>    Parent net profit			  554.4   vs 534.6</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the German carmaker is Bayerische</p>
<p>Motoren Werke AG. On January 30, it reported group revenue in</p>
<p>1996 climbed 13.3 percent to 52.27 billion marks. Analysts had</p>
<p>forecasts BMW would report a net profit of around 800 million</p>
<p>marks.</p>
<p>--Scott Miller, Frankfurt Newsroom + 49 69 756525</p>
</text>
